  "operative_text": "NEW SECTION Sec. 1 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (4) \"Large capacity magazine\" means an ammunition feeding device with the capacity to accept more than ten rounds of ammunition, or any conversion kit, part, or combination of parts, from which such a device can be assembled if those parts are in the possession or under the control of the same person, but shall not be construed to include any of the following:\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (1) No person in this state may manufacture, possess, distribute, import, transfer, sell, offer for sale, purchase, or otherwise transfer any assault weapon or large capacity magazine except as authorized in this section.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 2 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (4) A person who violates this section is guilty of a class C felony punishable under chapter  9A.20 RCW.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 3 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (1) Except as provided in subsection (2) of this section, a person shall not:\nNEW SECTION Sec. 3 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (a) Transport an assault weapon into Washington state; or\nNEW SECTION Sec. 3 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (b) Possess, sell, offer to sell, transfer, purchase, or receive an assault weapon.\nNEW SECTION Sec. 3 (new RCW chapter 9.41): (2)(a) A person who lawfully possessed, has a purchase order for, or completed an application to purchase an assault weapon before January 1, 2021, and who has registered the assault weapon with the Washington state patrol may:"
